  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Autocomplete Feature**\n\nOkay, I\'m working on that autocomplete feature. The core focus right now is designing the UI dropdown component, ensuring it\'s reusable and fully accessible. This will integrate neatly with the `GlobalSearchBar.tsx`, making it efficient for suggesting categories and keywords.\n\n\n**Defining Autocomplete Features**\n\nI\'ve been defining the required features for this autocomplete implementation. It needs to trigger upon focus or typing, suggesting both categories/subcategories (with paths and icons) and popular keywords, filtered by the query. Matching should highlight or bold substrings. I\'m considering listing title suggestions as well.\n\n\n**Implementing Autocomplete Behavior**\n\nI\'m now implementing the autocomplete behavior with two key triggers: focus (displaying popular searches and main categories) and typing (filtering suggestions). For empty queries, I\'ll show \"Popular searches\" and \"Main categories\" for discovery. I am incorporating keyboard navigation (up/down arrows, Enter, Escape) and ARIA attributes for accessibility. The visual grouping is defined to include section headers with clear visual cues and click functionality.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 203112942
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
