    thinking: "**Examining Initial Element**\n\nI\'m now investigating the specific element identified by the complex CSS selector provided. My focus has shifted back to `HomePage.tsx` for further context.\n\n\n**Analyzing Hero Section Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `HomePage.tsx` file, specifically the hero section\'s structure. I\'ve noted the use of grid columns and the balanced two-column layout. The `GlobalSearchBar` component and inline quick search trending tags have been identified as key elements within this hero section. This will influence how I model the UI.\n\n\n**Dissecting Popular Searches**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"Popular Searches\" section within the hero component. Specifically, I\'m examining how these popular search terms are presented. I\'m noting the use of buttons and their interaction with the `navigate` function, as well as the \'Map\' button and its link. The visual styling is key to understanding the UI structure and overall intent.\n\n\n**Observing Page Structure**\n\nI\'m now examining the `HomePage.tsx` DOM structure, noting that the hero, categories grid, and fresh listings are all enclosed in `<section>` tags. This contrasts with my earlier observations about divs. This new analysis will help with better mapping of the application\'s overall structure, and a look at `SearchPage.tsx` will provide additional context.\n\n\n**Investigating Search Page Structure**\n\nI\'m now analyzing `SearchPage.tsx` and the main content area. I\'m focusing on the `div` structure within the main element. I\'ve noted the `GlobalSearchBar` and active filters component, followed by the `<CategoryFilterRail />`. A responsive grid layout seems to be in place for the filtering components, with a focus on the left-side filters. I am specifically interested in how filters are presented, including the header and the \"Masquer\" button. I am remembering the previous request regarding the dropdown selection.\n\n\n**Tracing Filter Containers**\n\nI\