    prompt_sections {
      title: "skills"
      content: "<skills>\n# Skills\n\nYou can use specialized \'skills\' to help you with tasks. Each skill has a name and a description listed below.\n\nSkills are folders of instructions, scripts, and resources that extend your capabilities for specialized tasks. Each skill folder contains:\n- **SKILL.md** (required): The main instruction file with YAML frontmatter (name, description) and detailed markdown instructions\n\nMore complex skills may include additional directories and files as needed, for example:\n- **scripts/** - Helper scripts and utilities that extend your capabilities\n- **examples/** - Reference implementations and usage patterns\n- **resources/** - Additional files, templates, or assets the skill may reference\n\nImportant:\n\n- When a skill matches the user\'s request or seems relevant, this is a BLOCKING\n  REQUIREMENT: You MUST use the `view_file` tool on the SKILL.md file to read\n  its full instructions BEFORE generating any other response about the task.\n  Once you have read the instructions, follow them exactly as documented.\n\n\nAvailable skills:\n- cloudsql-execute-sql (/skills/system_skills/cloudsql-execute-sql/SKILL.md): Executes SQL statements on the Cloud SQL instance. This tool is designed for data query language (DQL) and data manipulation language (DML) operations, such as querying existing data, seeding databases, and debugging.\n\nDo NOT use this skill for:\n  - Applications that do not use Cloud SQL as their database.\n\nImportant Guidelines:\n  - Do not use this tool for data definition language (DDL) operations (e.g., creating or altering tables); these should be handled by the ORM. Exception: You may use this tool to install PostgreSQL extensions, which the ORM does not support.\n  - Do not use this tool for data control language (DCL) operations.\n  - Do not use this tool to create, update, or delete databases or database users.\n  - Avoid destructive actions like dropping tables or databases.\n  - Use \"sql_statement\" as the argument name. Do not use \"sql\".\n- cloudsql-setup (/skills/system_skills/cloudsql-setup/SKILL.md): Provisions a relational Cloud SQL (PostgreSQL) database and configures Firebase Authentication together. Do NOT use this skill if only Firebase Authentication is requested without a relational database.\n\nUse this skill ONLY if at least one of the following conditions is met:\n* The user explicitly requests PostgreSQL, SQL, Relational database.\n* The user explicitly requests Cloud SQL, Supabase, Neon, RDS, Aurora.\n\nCapabilities of the provisioned Cloud SQL instance with Developer edition:\n* Near-instant provisioning (~2 seconds).\n* Scale-to-zero capabilities with a free tier for cost savings.\n- cloudsql-update-schema (/skills/system_skills/cloudsql-update-schema/SKILL.md): Updates the Cloud SQL database schema for the app based on the schema defined in src/db/schema.ts and the configuration in src/db/drizzle.config.ts.\nUse this skill if any of the following happen:\n  - The user requests to update their Cloud SQL database schema\n  - Changes are made to the src/db/schema.ts file\n  - Changes are made to the src/db/drizzle.config.ts file\n- firebase-integration (/skills/system_skills/firebase-skill/SKILL.md): Integrate Firebase (Firestore and Auth) into applications, generate secure rules, and handle errors.\n\nUse this skill in the following scenarios:\n* New Backend Requirements: When the user requests to add a database, persistent storage, or user authentication to their application and Firestore with Firebase Authentication is a good fit\n* Schema Design: When defining the data structure for a new feature or application using Firestore.\n* Security Hardening: When generating or auditing Firestore security rules to prevent unauthorized access and data leaks.\n* Troubleshooting: When debugging \"Missing or insufficient permissions\" errors or other Firebase-related failures.\n* SDK Integration: When adding Firebase initialization and data fetching code to a React or TypeScript application.\n\nDo NOT use this skill for:\n* General GCP resource management outside of the specific Firebase tools provided.\n* Applications that do not use or intend to use Firebase as their backend.\n- focus-mode (/skills/system_skills/focus_mode/SKILL.md): Instructions for responding to UI element selection (CSS selectors).\n- gemini-api (/skills/system_skills/gemini_api/SKILL.md): Provides model selection guidance and coding patterns for the @google/genai TypeScript SDK. Use when the application requires AI capabilities (e.g., text/image generation, smart features) or when the task involves implementing an \"AI-powered\" feature. The model should prefer this modern SDK over legacy alternatives. Do NOT use for general discussions about AI without implementation intent. Covers model aliases, streaming, chat, function calling, search and maps grounding, Live API, TTS, and API key handling.\n- gemini-interactions-api (/skills/system_skills/gemini_interactions_api/SKILL.md): Provides coding patterns for the @google/genai TypeScript SDK. Covers using the Interactions API for the Antigravity agent, Deep Research agent, Omni models (Omni Flash), and general model capabilities (text, image, speech generation), as well as other specialized APIs for music (Lyria) and real-time audio (Live API) in a server-side context. Note that Omni models and Agents are only available via the Interactions API, not with standard generateContent. Use when user requests the Interactions API, Antigravity agent, Deep Research agent, or Omni models.\n- github-import-migration (/skills/system_skills/github_import_migration/SKILL.md): Execute-First migration for GitHub repositories imported into AI Studio. Triages projects and routes to the appropriate self-contained migration reference. Supports Web (Node.js) and Android (Kotlin/Compose) runtimes.\n- github-import-rewrite (/skills/system_skills/github_import_rewrite/SKILL.md): Cross-framework rewrite for GitHub repositories imported into AI Studio. Rewrites the imported project from its source framework to a different target framework while preserving core features and business logic.\n- google-maps-platform (/skills/system_skills/google_maps_platform/SKILL.md): Provides architectural guidance and generates production-ready code for applications using Google Maps Platform. Specializes in building software with location APIs and SDKs such as Places API (New), Routes API, and Address Validation API, utilizing modern React patterns. Dynamically retrieves documentation and code context via the rpc_action tool to provide accurate implementation details. Use this skill when you need to implement any location-based application task or solution, such as a Store Locator, Checkout/shipping experiences with address validation, data visualizations on maps, or directions routing logic in a React application.\n- image-generation (/skills/system_skills/image_generation/SKILL.md): Use when the application needs to generate or update images \342\200\224 hero banners, illustrations, icons, backgrounds, avatars, product photos, or any visual asset. Covers image selection strategy (using tools vs assets vs placeholders) and runtime generation using Gemini models.\n- oauth-integration (/skills/system_skills/oauth/SKILL.md): Guidelines for implementing OAuth flows (Strava, GitHub, etc.) in the AI Studio preview environment. Use when the user requests OAuth, login with third-party services, or popup-based authentication. Covers iframe constraints, cookie configuration, and redirect URI setup.\n- real-time-and-multi-user (/skills/system_skills/realtime_guidelines/SKILL.md): Guidelines for implementing real-time features, WebSockets, and collaborative canvases. Use when the app requires chat, live collaboration, multiplayer games, or notifications. Covers server-authoritative state, event-based communication, and canvas library selection (Konva, Fabric.js).\n- shadcn-ui (/skills/system_skills/shadcn/SKILL.md): Guidelines for using shadcn/ui components and CLI. Use ONLY when the user requests shadcn or shadcn/ui. Covers initialization, adding components, community registries, and theming.\n- workspace-integration (/skills/system_skills/workspace_integration/SKILL.md): Integrate Google Workspace APIs (Drive, Docs, Sheets, Slides, Calendar, Gmail, Chat, Meet, Forms, Classroom, Tasks, Keep, People, Picker) into the application. Use when the user wants to read, write, or search Workspace data. Requires OAuth configuration via the set_up_oauth and remove_oauth tools.\n\n</skills>"
      metadata {
        source_type: PROMPT_SECTION_SOURCE_TYPE_RAW
      }
      token_type: TOKEN_TYPE_SYSTEM_PROMPT
      token_source: TOKEN_SOURCE_SYSTEM
    }
    prompt_sections {
      title: "user_rules"
      content: "<user_rules>\nThe following are user-defined rules that you MUST ALWAYS FOLLOW WITHOUT ANY EXCEPTION. These rules take precedence over any following instructions.\nReview them carefully and always take them into account when you generate responses and code:\n\n<RULE[AGENTS_md]>\n# AGENTS.md \342\200\224 Directives & Contrats d\'Architecture Shongre\n\nCe document constitue le **contrat d\'impl\303\251mentation faisant autorit\303\251** pour tous les agents IA et d\303\251veloppeurs intervenant sur le d\303\251p\303\264t Shongre. Tout code produit doit se conformer strictement \303\240 ces r\303\250gles sans exception.\n\n---\n\n## 1. P\303\251rim\303\250tre & Fronti\303\250re des Fichiers\n\n1. **Tout le code et la configuration frontend doivent r\303\251sider sous `/frontend`** :\n   - `frontend/src/`\n   - `frontend/package.json`\n   - `frontend/vite.config.ts`\n   - `frontend/tsconfig.json`\n   - `frontend/index.html`\n   - `frontend/bin/`\n2. **Ne jamais cr\303\251er de fichiers frontend \303\240 la racine du d\303\251p\303\264t** (pas de `src/`, `public/`, `dist/`, ou `package.json` \303\240 la racine).\n3. **Commandes autoris\303\251es** :\n   - Ex\303\251cuter depuis `frontend/` (ex: `cd frontend && npm test`) ou via les cibles du `Makefile` \303\240 la racine (ex: `make check`, `make dev`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Pr\303\251servation du Baseline & Discipline Git\n\n1. **V\303\251rifier l\'\303\251tat avant toute intervention** :\n   ```bash\n   git status\n   git diff\n   ```\n2. **Op\303\251rations destructives formellement interdites** :\n   - Ne jamais ex\303\251cuter `git reset --hard` ou `git clean -fd`.\n   - Traiter l\'arbre de travail existant comme intentionnel et pr\303\251server les modifications non valid\303\251es.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Table des Sources de V\303\251rit\303\251 Canoniques\n\n| Domaine / Pr\303\251occupation | Emplacement Source Faisant Autorit\303\251 | R\303\250gle d\'Acc\303\250s pour les Vues / Features |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Taxonomie & Attributs** | `frontend/src/domains/taxonomy/taxonomy.data.ts` | Consommer via `taxonomyService` ou `CANONICAL_TAXONOMY` / `ATTRIBUTE_REGISTRY`. Ne jamais recr\303\251er de listes de cat\303\251gories locales. |\n| **Design System & Tokens** | `frontend/src/design-system/` et `src/index.css` | R\303\251utiliser les primitives (`Button`, `Modal`, `Badge`, `FormField`, `CategoryIcon`). Utiliser les classes de tokens s\303\251mantiques. |\n| **Configuration March\303\251s** | `frontend/src/domains/market/market.resolver.ts` | Consommer via `marketResolver.getEffectiveMarketConfig(code)`. Ne jamais coder en dur de fallbacks manuels `market \\|\\| FR`. |\n| **S\303\251curit\303\251 & Permissions** | `frontend/src/security/authorization.service.ts` | Consommer via `authorizationService.can(user, perm)` ou le hook `useAuthorization()`. |\n| **Mon\303\251tisation & Boosts** | `frontend/src/configuration/plans.config.ts` | Consommer `LISTING_BOOSTS`, `PRO_SUBSCRIPTION_PLANS` et `TRANSACTION_COMMISSIONS`. |\n| **Calculs de S\303\251questre** | `frontend/src/domains/transaction/transaction.service.ts` | Utiliser `calculateOrderTotal()` et `transactionService`. |\n| **Acc\303\250s aux Donn\303\251es** | `frontend/src/repositories/` | Passer obligatoirement par `listingRepository`, `userRepository`, `transactionRepository` ou `messagingRepository`. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. R\303\250gle Anti-Duplication : \"Un Concept = Une Seule Impl\303\251mentation\"\n\n1. **Recherche pr\303\251alable obligatoire** :\n   - Avant de cr\303\251er un composant, un hook, un service, un type ou un utilitaire, inspecter le codebase pour v\303\251rifier s\'il existe d\303\251j\303\240 un \303\251quivalent.\n2. **Interdiction des suffixes de duplication** :\n   - Ne jamais cr\303\251er de fichiers temporaires ou doublons nomm\303\251s `ListingCardV2`, `SellerPageNew`, `PublicationFinal`, `NewModal.tsx`.\n   - Si une refonte est n\303\251cessaire, migrer tous les consommateurs existants, valider, puis supprimer l\'ancienne impl\303\251mentation.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Primitives du Design System & R\303\250gles de Style\n\n1. **Primitives Canoniques** (`src/design-system/primitives/`) :\n   - `Button`, `IconButton`, `ActionLink`, `BackLink`\n   - `Badge`, `Notice`, `StatePanel`\n   - `FormField`, `Input`, `Textarea`, `Select`, `Checkbox`, `Radio`\n   - `Modal`, `ConfirmModal`, `Drawer`, `Tabs`\n   - `CategoryIcon`\n2. **Tokens CSS** :\n   - Toujours utiliser les tokens s\303\251mantiques d\303\251finis dans `src/index.css` (`bg-primary`, `text-primary`, `border-border-base`, `bg-bg-subtle`, `shadow-xs`).\n   - Ne pas introduire de styles inline arbitraires ou de valeurs hexad\303\251cimales non r\303\251f\303\251renc\303\251es.\n\n---\n\n## 6. R\303\250gles M\303\251tier Cl\303\251s\n\n### 6.1 Taxonomie Unique, Publication & Libell\303\251s Compacts (`shortLabel`)\n- La publication d\'annonce est **enti\303\250rement pilot\303\251e par la taxonomie** (`taxonomy.data.ts`).\n- Les formulaires d\'attributs s\'adaptent dynamiquement selon la cat\303\251gorie s\303\251lectionn\303\251e (`attributesSchema`).\n- Ne jamais comparer des cha\303\256nes fran\303\247aises de pr\303\251sentation (ex: `if (category === \'Voitures\')`) pour orienter la logique m\303\251tier ; utiliser les slugs canoniques (`categorySlug === \'vehicles\'`) ou les capacit\303\251s de listing.\n- **R\303\250gle `shortLabel`** : `label` / `name` est le nom canonique complet faisant autorit\303\251. `shortLabel` est un alias compact optionnel r\303\251serv\303\251 aux interfaces contraintes (tiroirs mobiles, grilles d\'accueil, filtres). Toujours r\303\251soudre les libell\303\251s via `getTaxonomyLabel(node, \'compact\' | \'full\')`. Ne jamais d\303\251river d\'identifiants, de slugs ou de logique m\303\251tier \303\240 partir de `shortLabel`. Ne jamais cr\303\251er de tables locales d\'alias dans les composants.\n\n### 6.2 Syst\303\250me Multi-March\303\251s & H\303\251ritage France\n- La France (`FR`) est le **march\303\251 de r\303\251f\303\251rence canonique**.\n- Pour tout march\303\251 \303\251tranger (`BE`, `CH`, `LU`, `DE`, `ES`), les param\303\250tres non surcharg\303\251s h\303\251ritent automatiquement de la France.\n- Ne jamais \303\251crire `market.protectionFee || france.protectionFee`, car une valeur `0` ou `false` peut \303\252tre une surcharge explicite valide. Utiliser `getEffectiveMarketConfig()`.\n\n### 6.3 Transactions : Achat Direct vs R\303\251servation\n- **Achat Direct (`DIRECT_PURCHASE`)** : S\303\251questre total du montant + frais de livraison $\\to$ exp\303\251dition ou remise avec validation PIN $\\to$ d\303\251blocage automatique des fonds.\n- **R\303\251servation (`RESERVATION`)** : S\303\251questre d\'un acompte $\\to$ rendez-vous physique $\\to$ paiement du solde de la main \303\240 la main.\n- Ces deux flux sont distincts et ne doivent pas \303\252tre confondus.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Responsabilit\303\251 des Composants & Architecture des Donn\303\251es\n\n1. **Pages = Composition** :\n   - Les pages du dossier `features/` composent les composants visuels et les hooks.\n   - Les calculs m\303\251tier lourds, validations d\'\303\251tat et r\303\251solutions fiscales doivent r\303\251sider dans les services de domaine (`domains/`).\n2. **Isolation des Donn\303\251es de D\303\251monstration** :\n   - Les jeux de donn\303\251es de d\303\251monstration (`src/mocks/initialDemoData.ts`) sont la propri\303\251t\303\251 exclusive de la couche `repositories/` et `storageService`.\n   - Ne jamais importer directement des tableaux bruts de fixtures dans les composants de page.\n3. **Propri\303\251t\303\251 de l\'\303\211tat** :\n   - **URL (`searchParams`)** : Source de v\303\251rit\303\251 pour la recherche, les filtres, la pagination et les onglets partageables.\n   - **Repositories** : Cache des ressources et \303\251tat persistant simul\303\251.\n   - **Contextes React** : Uniquement pour l\'\303\251tat global authentique (`AuthProvider`, `ToastProvider`, `MarketProvider`).\n\n---\n\n## 8. Responsivit\303\251 & Accessibilit\303\251 (a11y)\n\n1. **Multi-\303\251crans obligatoire** :\n   - Toute modification d\'interface doit \303\252tre valid\303\251e sur mobile (375px), tablette (768px) et desktop (1280px).\n   - Aucun d\303\251bordement horizontal (`overflow-x`) non d\303\251sir\303\251.\n2. **Accessibilit\303\251** :\n   - Utiliser des balises HTML s\303\251mantiques (`button`, `main`, `nav`, `header`, `section`).\n   - Assurer le focus clavier visible et les labels explicites sur tous les champs de formulaire.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Validation & D\303\251finition du \"Fini\" (Definition of Done)\n\nAvant de consid\303\251rer une t\303\242che comme termin\303\251e, ex\303\251cuter obligatoirement la suite compl\303\250te :\n\n```bash\nmake check\n```\n\nCe script valide s\303\251quentiellement les 3 \303\251tapes critiques :\n1. `npm run lint` (`tsc --noEmit` \342\200\224 **0 erreur de typage**).\n2. `npm test` (`vitest run` \342\200\224 **100% des tests unitaires passants**).\n3. `npm run build` (`vite build` \342\200\224 **bundle de production optimis\303\251 et sans erreur**).\n\nNe jamais contourner ces v\303\251rifications avec des `@ts-ignore`, des `any` abusifs ou en d\303\251sactivant des tests.\n</RULE[AGENTS_md]>\n</user_rules>"
